Another option (though, admittedly, not open to all classes) which
I've exercised is "kill him from a distance".  I had a gnomish wizard
stand outside his room and lob fireballs at where I knew he was; he
never saw me, never moved, and died fairly quickly.  You could
probably do something similar with a boulder fort and magic missile
wands (or other ranged attacks), for instance.

Point being, Vlad is no longer an "ignorable" monster, and everyone
will have to find their own preferred methods for taking him out with
the various classes.  You've found some options which don't work well
(such as dust-E and bear traps); you've also listed some that
definitely will; others have suggested some that worked for them, and
which you may be able to incorporate into your play style.  Give it
some thought, and then give it a chance.

